# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "A lar: address in prose leaves trailing punctuation, starts after an underline mark, and reads in an unquoted value"

# Wave-2 cold readers, 2026-11-01, each inherited from 3.0.1. An address in a sentence left the
# sentence's full stop or closing parenthesis inside its path; `__lar:…__` read no address, because
# `\b` finds no boundary after `_`; and an unquoted `a=lar:…` call value read as a bare string.

x see lar:///a.b.c/x/y. Next sentence.
#                    ^ variable.other.constant.path.lar.memetic-wikitext
#                     ^ - meta.uri.lar.memetic-wikitext

x (lar:///a.b.c/x) and on
#               ^ variable.other.constant.path.lar.memetic-wikitext
#                ^ - meta.uri.lar.memetic-wikitext

x lar:///a.b.c, then more
#            ^ entity.name.tag.dynamic.lar.memetic-wikitext
#             ^ - meta.uri.lar.memetic-wikitext

x lar:///a.b.c/x.y/z mid-path dots stay
#              ^^^ variable.other.constant.path.lar.memetic-wikitext

x __lar:///a.b.c/x__ tail
#   ^^^ support.constant.scheme.lar.memetic-wikitext
#          ^ entity.name.tag.heading.lar.memetic-wikitext

<<m a=lar:///a.b.c/x>>
#     ^^^ support.constant.scheme.lar.memetic-wikitext
